        "original_id": "38ca3b18-8c8d-5f1b-8dc4-0b45a60e93a5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Zenon B. Lukosius, elder Moore\n- Military Units: U.S. Navy, Kriegsmarine\n- Vessels: German submarine U-505, Type IXC U-boat\n- Works: Playing with the Enemy\n- Events: World War II, capture of U-505, prisoner of war detention\n\nFacts:\n- German submarine U-505 was a German Type IXC U-boat built for Nazi Germany's Kriegsmarine during World War II.\n- In 1944, Zenon B. Lukosius was a member of the U.S. Navy crew that captured the German submarine U-505.\n- Zenon B. Lukosius was a Lithuanian-American World War II veteran who lived from August 24, 1918 to August 12, 2006.\n- Playing with the Enemy takes its title from elder Moore's time as a guard in a top-secret prisoner of war camp that held the crew of the captured German submarine U-505.",
